All of them are compatible with GPL-3.0. Only pydicom and requests are pinned; their own
dependencies are the versions pip picks when the image is built.

Test scripts only (bridge/q_test.py, bridge/storetest.py, not in the image, installed by
hand when needed):

  pynetdicom           any                MIT-style

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Orthanc
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The image server is Orthanc, a separate program by other authors: core GPL-3.0-or-later;
the DICOMweb, Stone Web Viewer and Orthanc Explorer 2 plugins AGPL-3.0-or-later; the
worklists plugin GPL-3.0-or-later. docker-compose.yml runs the unmodified official image
orthancteam/orthanc (tag pinned there; 26.9.1 at the time of writing) and configures it with
environment variables. The bridge, the scripts and Bethesda EMR talk to it only over its
REST API, the DICOM protocol and the worklist folder. No Orthanc code is in this
repository, linked into it or derived from it.

This repository does not distribute Orthanc: Docker pulls it from Docker Hub. Whoever
distributes the image (for example in an offline install kit) must meet the GPL/AGPL terms
for it, including the offer of its corresponding source:
  https://orthanc.uclouvain.be/downloads/          (Orthanc source releases)
  https://github.com/orthanc-team/orthanc-builder  (how the Docker image is built)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Bethesda CD (bethesda-cd/)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bethesda-CD.exe and VIEWER.EXE are compiled with the C# compiler of the .NET Framework 4.8
(csc.exe) and reference only Windows system components: System.Windows.Forms,
System.Drawing, System.IO.Compression, System.Web.Extensions, Microsoft.CSharp and the
IMAPI2 burning service (COM). These are System Libraries in the sense of GPLv3 section 1.
No NuGet package or other third-party library is used. The viewer's lossless JPEG and RLE
decoders are written for this project from the public standards (ITU-T T.81, DICOM PS3.5).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Other files
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The icons (bethesda-pacs.ico, bethesda-cd/icon/Bethesda-CD.ico, drawn by
bethesda-cd/icon/make-icon.ps1) are the project's own. The Windows scripts use only
PowerShell 5.1 and Windows. No fonts or third-party images are included.
